// THE WITNESS-SET IDENTITY JOIN (gunbc.plans.source_layout_authority, C4 admission). A layout sweep
// changes where witness files live and what their modules are called, and it must change nothing about
// WHICH witnesses the floor discovers. A count cannot say that: a sweep that dropped a marker from a
// thousand files and added a thousand elsewhere leaves the total where it was. So the admission is an
// identity join. The set the discovery producer enrols before the sweep, carried through the sweep's own
// rename map, must equal the set it enrols after, row by row on (entry, function) with the row's label
// and live-tree disposition unchanged.
//
// THE SUBJECT IS THE TEST-MARKED DECLARATION. A test is a declaration carrying the authored `test`
// marker and nothing else: no file name, no stem, no text scan identifies one. So the after-side
// observation is built from the marker alone -- layout_witness_observe reads every governed file's
// marked names from the v2 marker channel (the capture normalize runs beside lowering, read off the
// parse tree by v2.compiler.module_acquisition acquisition_test_markers) and hands them to the real
// producer as supplied values. The before-side is whatever the retired convention enrolled, which is what the floor
// actually ran; a member the old convention enrolled that carries no marker is a ROW_LOST difference,
// listed and never absorbed. A row the join does not list as preserved is either a claim the change deleted
// or wrote, or a real claim that is owed its marker, and the join cannot tell which from the two
// observations: the caller can, from the sources, and declares the rows the change deletes with their
// declaration and the rows it writes. A declared row is still reported beside its difference; an undeclared
// one is red.
//
// A ROW IS PAIRED BY CONTENT AS WELL AS BY NAME. A preserved (entry, function) says the claim is still
// enrolled; it does not say the claim still says what it said. The observation therefore carries each
// marked declaration's CONTENT beside its name -- the structural identity of its parse, which the marker
// reader hands over with the names (v2.compiler.module_acquisition acquisition_test_markers) -- and a
// preserved row whose content differs is ROW_BODY_CHANGED, red. A sweep that rewrites the names a body
// cites changes its content, and the join does not know the rename map's effect on a body (a second
// rewriter would be a second authority): the caller declares each changed row with the content it was and
// the content it became (`entry<TAB>function<TAB>was<TAB>now`, the entry the old tree's path), reported
// beside the row as ROW_BODY_CHANGED_DECLARED. A declaration binds both digests, so a body edited a second
// time is red again, and a declaration that excuses no changed row is red (ROW_BODY_PIN_UNUSED): the
// list can only shrink.
//
// EVERY EXPLANATION IS EXACT IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. A finding is excused only by a declaration that names it (a
// path, an (entry, function) key, a pair of digests, a refusal's file under its exact cause), never by a
// pattern, a directory, a count or a reason, so no declaration reaches a row or a file it does not name. The
// converse holds as well: a declaration no finding used (it names a file still present, a file that held no
// enrolled row, a row that was neither lost nor gained, a file the channel read) is red
// (DECLARATION_UNUSED), as is one stated twice (DECLARATION_DUPLICATED). Every old row therefore ends
// preserved, red, or attached to exactly one declared mechanism, and every declared mechanism is attached to
// something the two trees actually show. The per-mechanism tallies a report quotes are the DISPOSITION lines
// this instrument prints, counted from the findings and never typed beside them.
//
// WHAT IS NOT OBSERVED. The producer is given no owned-data records here, exactly as
// v2.compiler.effect_demand_floor_join effect_demand_floor_join_live gives it none: a Bool-valued owned
// data witness is enrolled by the host's own scan, which has no substrate producer yet. The join
// therefore establishes the set of test-marked declarations and nothing over a data witness. What it
// establishes is that the set the channel reports is unchanged across the sweep, both trees read through
// that one channel; it is not a second, independent reading of what a person would mark.
//
// A FILE THE MARKER CHANNEL CANNOT READ IS A LOCATED OBSERVATION, NOT AN ABORT AND NOT AN EMPTY LIST. A
// governed file the v2 grammar refuses has no marker fact, so the producer is not asked about it and the
// observation records it as UNREAD with the cause the channel refused with. Its old rows are then neither
// lost nor preserved but unobserved (RowUnread), and red unless gunbc.parse_population_refusals declares
// that file under that exact cause: the same declaration that excuses the population parse excuses the
// markers, so the loss is one drop and the capability that restores it (a grammar that parses the file)
// restores both. A file the channel reads but the declaration still names is the population parse's red,
// not this join's.
//
// THE RENAME MAP IS LAYOUT_MIGRATION'S OWN PLAN (layout_plan_report on the pre-sweep tree), not a second
// mapping derived from the two trees: a derived mapping would agree with whatever the sweep did. A path
// the plan does not name is carried through unchanged.
//
// A FILE REMOVED OR ADDED IS NOT A SWEEP EFFECT AND IS NEVER ABSORBED. A file holding rows with no
// counterpart is red unless the run declares its removal, and a declared removal is a path the caller
// names from the independent git record of the change. Rows in an added file are reported as introduced,
// never as a pre-image-less match.

// ---- the observation -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// One line per fact. `ROW<TAB>entry<TAB>function<TAB>label<TAB>live<TAB>body` is an enrolled witness and
// the content of the declaration that enrols it;
// `FILE<TAB>path` is a tracked source file, the population the file-grain check reads;
// `UNREAD<TAB>path<TAB>cause` is a governed file the marker channel refused, located by the cause it
// refused with. An unread file has no marker fact, so it is never walked and never read as an
// unmarked one.
type ObservedRow {
  entry: String
  function: String
  label: String
  live: String
  body: String
}

type UnreadFile {
  path: String
  cause: String
}

type Observation {
  rows: List<ObservedRow>
  files: List<String>
  unread: List<UnreadFile>
  malformed: List<String>
}

fn live_label(disposition: LiveTreeDisposition) -> String {
  match disposition {
    ReadsLiveTree => "ReadsLiveTree"
    SubstrateInputsOnly => "SubstrateInputsOnly"
  }
}

fn observed_row_line(row: FloorDiscoveryRow, body: String) -> String {
  join(["ROW", row.entry, row.function, row.label, live_label(disposition: row.reads_live_tree), body], "\t")
}

fn observed_file_line(path: String) -> String {
  concat("FILE\t", path)
}

fn observed_unread_line(unread: UnreadFile) -> String {
  join(["UNREAD", unread.path, unread.cause], "\t")
}

fn field_of(fields: List<String>, index: Int) -> String {
  let element = fields[index]
  match element {
    Present { value: v } => v
    Absent => ""
  }
}

fn line_is_row(line: String) -> Bool {
  let fields = split(s: line, delimiter: "\t")
  field_of(fields: fields, index: 0) == "ROW" && count(fields) == 6
}

fn line_is_file(line: String) -> Bool {
  let fields = split(s: line, delimiter: "\t")
  field_of(fields: fields, index: 0) == "FILE" && count(fields) == 2
}

fn line_is_unread(line: String) -> Bool {
  let fields = split(s: line, delimiter: "\t")
  field_of(fields: fields, index: 0) == "UNREAD" && count(fields) == 3
}

fn observed_unread_of(line: String) -> UnreadFile {
  let fields = split(s: line, delimiter: "\t")
  UnreadFile { path: field_of(fields: fields, index: 1), cause: field_of(fields: fields, index: 2) }
}

fn observed_row_of(line: String) -> ObservedRow {
  let fields = split(s: line, delimiter: "\t")
  ObservedRow {
    entry: field_of(fields: fields, index: 1),
    function: field_of(fields: fields, index: 2),
    label: field_of(fields: fields, index: 3),
    live: field_of(fields: fields, index: 4),
    body: field_of(fields: fields, index: 5)
  }
}

fn observation_of(text: String) -> Observation {
  let lines = split(s: text, delimiter: "\n") |> filter(l => l != "")
  Observation {
    rows: lines |> filter(l => line_is_row(line: l)) |> map(l => observed_row_of(line: l)),
    files: lines |> filter(l => line_is_file(line: l)) |> map(l => field_of(fields: split(s: l, delimiter: "\t"), index: 1)),
    unread: lines |> filter(l => line_is_unread(line: l)) |> map(l => observed_unread_of(line: l)),
    malformed: lines |> filter(l => !line_is_row(line: l) && !line_is_file(line: l) && !line_is_unread(line: l))
  }
}

fn row_key(entry: String, function: String) -> String {
  concat(entry, "\t", function)
}

fn line_is_row_key(line: String) -> Bool {
  count(split(s: line, delimiter: "\t")) == 2
}

fn row_value(row: ObservedRow) -> String {
  concat(row.label, "\t", row.live)
}

fn row_index(rows: List<ObservedRow>) -> Map<String, String> {
  fold(rows, init: empty_map(), f: (index, row) => map_insert(m: index, key: row_key(entry: row.entry, function: row.function), value: row_value(row: row)))
}

fn body_index(rows: List<ObservedRow>) -> Map<String, String> {
  fold(rows, init: empty_map(), f: (index, row) => map_insert(m: index, key: row_key(entry: row.entry, function: row.function), value: row.body))
}

fn body_of(index: Map<String, String>, key: String) -> String {
  match map_lookup(m: index, key: key) {
    Present { value: body } => body
    Absent => ""
  }
}

fn body_present(index: Map<String, String>, key: String) -> Bool {
  match map_lookup(m: index, key: key) {
    Present { value: _ } => true
    Absent => false
  }
}

fn path_index(paths: List<String>) -> Map<String, Bool> {
  fold(paths, init: empty_map(), f: (index, path) => map_insert(m: index, key: path, value: true))
}

fn path_present(index: Map<String, Bool>, path: String) -> Bool {
  match map_lookup(m: index, key: path) {
    Present { value: _ } => true
    Absent => false
  }
}

// ---- the rename map ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// layout_migration_map plan_digest_line: `old_path<TAB>new_path<TAB>new_module<TAB>category`. The
// summary lines the plan report leads with carry no tab and are not edges.
type PlanEdges {
  forward: Map<String, String>
  paths: List<String>
  malformed: List<String>
}

fn plan_line_is_edge(line: String) -> Bool {
  count(split(s: line, delimiter: "\t")) == 4
}

fn plan_line_is_summary(line: String) -> Bool {
  count(split(s: line, delimiter: "\t")) == 1
}

fn plan_edges_of(text: String) -> PlanEdges {
  let lines = split(s: text, delimiter: "\n") |> filter(l => l != "")
  let edges = lines |> filter(l => plan_line_is_edge(line: l))
  PlanEdges {
    forward: fold(edges, init: empty_map(), f: (index, l) => map_insert(m: index, key: field_of(fields: split(s: l, delimiter: "\t"), index: 0), value: field_of(fields: split(s: l, delimiter: "\t"), index: 1))),
    paths: edges |> map(l => field_of(fields: split(s: l, delimiter: "\t"), index: 0)),
    malformed: lines |> filter(l => !plan_line_is_edge(line: l) && !plan_line_is_summary(line: l))
  }
}

fn carried(forward: Map<String, String>, path: String) -> String {
  match map_lookup(m: forward, key: path) {
    Present { value: moved } => moved
    Absent => path
  }
}

// Each new path's pre-image, built over the old tracked files. A new path two old files reach is a
// collision, reported once, so the carry-through stays a function in both directions.
type Preimages {
  index: Map<String, String>
  collisions: List<String>
}

fn preimages_of(forward: Map<String, String>, old_files: List<String>) -> Preimages {
  fold(old_files, init: Preimages { index: empty_map(), collisions: [] }, f: fn(acc, old_path) {
    let new_path = carried(forward: forward, path: old_path)
    match map_lookup(m: acc.index, key: new_path) {
      Present { value: other } => Preimages { index: acc.index, collisions: concat(acc.collisions, [join([other, old_path, new_path], " + ")]) }
      Absent => Preimages { index: map_insert(m: acc.index, key: new_path, value: old_path), collisions: acc.collisions }
    }
  })
}

// ---- the join -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
type JoinFinding
  = RowPreserved
  | RowLost { entry: String, function: String, declared: Bool }
  | RowGained { entry: String, function: String, declared: Bool }
  | RowAltered { entry: String, function: String, was: String, now: String }
  | RowBodyChanged { entry: String, function: String, was: String, now: String, declared: Bool }
  | RowBodyPinUnused { entry: String, function: String }
  | RowUnread { entry: String, function: String, declared: Bool }
  | RowIntroduced { entry: String, function: String }
  | RowInRemovedFile { entry: String, function: String, declared: Bool }
  | FileRemoved { path: String }
  | FileAdded { path: String }
  | PlanStale { old_path: String }
  | PlanCollision { paths: String }
  | InputMalformed { source: String, line: String }
  | DeclarationUnused { kind: String, key: String }
  | DeclarationDuplicated { kind: String, key: String }

fn finding_is_red(finding: JoinFinding) -> Bool {
  match finding {
    RowPreserved => false
    RowLost { entry: _, function: _, declared: declared } => !declared
    RowGained { entry: _, function: _, declared: declared } => !declared
    RowAltered { entry: _, function: _, was: _, now: _ } => true
    RowBodyChanged { entry: _, function: _, was: _, now: _, declared: declared } => !declared
    RowBodyPinUnused { entry: _, function: _ } => true
    RowUnread { entry: _, function: _, declared: declared } => !declared
    RowIntroduced { entry: _, function: _ } => false
    RowInRemovedFile { entry: _, function: _, declared: declared } => !declared
    FileRemoved { path: _ } => false
    FileAdded { path: _ } => false
    PlanStale { old_path: _ } => true
    PlanCollision { paths: _ } => true
    InputMalformed { source: _, line: _ } => true
    DeclarationUnused { kind: _, key: _ } => true
    DeclarationDuplicated { kind: _, key: _ } => true
  }
}

// The disposition a finding carries, as its report names it. One function, read by the rendered line and by
// the disposition table, so the table counts what the report prints and not a second reading of it.
fn finding_kind(finding: JoinFinding) -> String {
  match finding {
    RowPreserved => "PRESERVED"
    RowLost { entry: _, function: _, declared: d } => if d { "ROW_LOST_DECLARED" } else { "ROW_LOST" }
    RowGained { entry: _, function: _, declared: d } => if d { "ROW_GAINED_DECLARED" } else { "ROW_GAINED" }
    RowAltered { entry: _, function: _, was: _, now: _ } => "ROW_ALTERED"
    RowBodyChanged { entry: _, function: _, was: _, now: _, declared: d } => if d { "ROW_BODY_CHANGED_DECLARED" } else { "ROW_BODY_CHANGED" }
    RowBodyPinUnused { entry: _, function: _ } => "ROW_BODY_PIN_UNUSED"
    RowUnread { entry: _, function: _, declared: d } => if d { "ROW_UNREAD_DECLARED" } else { "ROW_UNREAD" }
    RowIntroduced { entry: _, function: _ } => "ROW_INTRODUCED"
    RowInRemovedFile { entry: _, function: _, declared: d } => if d { "ROW_IN_REMOVED_FILE_DECLARED" } else { "ROW_IN_REMOVED_FILE" }
    FileRemoved { path: _ } => "FILE_REMOVED"
    FileAdded { path: _ } => "FILE_ADDED"
    PlanStale { old_path: _ } => "PLAN_STALE"
    PlanCollision { paths: _ } => "PLAN_COLLISION"
    InputMalformed { source: _, line: _ } => "INPUT_MALFORMED"
    DeclarationUnused { kind: _, key: _ } => "DECLARATION_UNUSED"
    DeclarationDuplicated { kind: _, key: _ } => "DECLARATION_DUPLICATED"
  }
}

// The fields a finding names after its disposition.
fn finding_subject(finding: JoinFinding) -> List<String> {
  match finding {
    RowPreserved => []
    RowLost { entry: e, function: f, declared: _ } => [e, f]
    RowGained { entry: e, function: f, declared: _ } => [e, f]
    RowAltered { entry: e, function: f, was: w, now: n } => [e, f, w, n]
    RowBodyChanged { entry: e, function: f, was: w, now: n, declared: _ } => [e, f, w, n]
    RowBodyPinUnused { entry: e, function: f } => [e, f]
    RowUnread { entry: e, function: f, declared: _ } => [e, f]
    RowIntroduced { entry: e, function: f } => [e, f]
    RowInRemovedFile { entry: e, function: f, declared: _ } => [e, f]
    FileRemoved { path: p } => [p]
    FileAdded { path: p } => [p]
    PlanStale { old_path: p } => [p]
    PlanCollision { paths: p } => [p]
    InputMalformed { source: s, line: l } => [s, l]
    DeclarationUnused { kind: k, key: key } => [k, key]
    DeclarationDuplicated { kind: k, key: key } => [k, key]
  }
}

fn finding_line(finding: JoinFinding) -> String {
  match finding {
    RowPreserved => "PRESERVED"
    _ => join(concat([if finding_is_red(finding: finding) { "RED" } else { "INFO" }, finding_kind(finding: finding)], finding_subject(finding: finding)), "\t")
  }
}

// An old row, carried through the plan, against the new observation. `unread` maps each new-side file the
// marker channel refused to whether that refusal is declared: a row whose file the channel could not read
// is neither lost nor preserved, it is unobserved, and it is red unless the refusal is a declared one.
fn old_row_finding(
  forward: Map<String, String>,
  new_files: Map<String, Bool>,
  new_rows: Map<String, String>,
  declared: Map<String, Bool>,
  removed_rows: Map<String, Bool>,
  unread: Map<String, Bool>,
  new_bodies: Map<String, String>,
  changes: Map<String, String>,
  row: ObservedRow
) -> JoinFinding {
  let moved = carried(forward: forward, path: row.entry)
  if !path_present(index: new_files, path: moved) {
    RowInRemovedFile { entry: row.entry, function: row.function, declared: path_present(index: declared, path: row.entry) }
  } else {
    match map_lookup(m: new_rows, key: row_key(entry: moved, function: row.function)) {
      Absent =>
        match map_lookup(m: unread, key: moved) {
          Present { value: covered } => RowUnread { entry: row.entry, function: row.function, declared: covered }
          Absent => RowLost { entry: row.entry, function: row.function, declared: path_present(index: removed_rows, path: row_key(entry: row.entry, function: row.function)) }
        }
      Present { value: now } =>
        if now == row_value(row: row) {
          body_finding(new_bodies: new_bodies, changes: changes, moved: moved, row: row)
        } else {
          RowAltered { entry: row.entry, function: row.function, was: row_value(row: row), now: now }
        }
    }
  }
}

// A preserved row against the content it had. The new content is the one observed at the carried path; a
// change is declared only by a pin that binds this row's old content to this row's new content.
fn body_finding(new_bodies: Map<String, String>, changes: Map<String, String>, moved: String, row: ObservedRow) -> JoinFinding {
  let now = body_of(index: new_bodies, key: row_key(entry: moved, function: row.function))
  if now == row.body {
    RowPreserved
  } else {
    RowBodyChanged {
      entry: row.entry,
      function: row.function,
      was: row.body,
      now: now,
      declared: body_change_declared(changes: changes, key: row_key(entry: row.entry, function: row.function), was: row.body, now: now)
    }
  }
}

fn body_change_declared(changes: Map<String, String>, key: String, was: String, now: String) -> Bool {
  match map_lookup(m: changes, key: key) {
    Present { value: pinned } => pinned == concat(was, "\t", now)
    Absent => false
  }
}

fn line_is_body_pin(line: String) -> Bool {
  count(split(s: line, delimiter: "\t")) == 4
}

fn body_pin_key(line: String) -> String {
  let fields = split(s: line, delimiter: "\t")
  row_key(entry: field_of(fields: fields, index: 0), function: field_of(fields: fields, index: 1))
}

fn body_pin_value(line: String) -> String {
  let fields = split(s: line, delimiter: "\t")
  concat(field_of(fields: fields, index: 2), "\t", field_of(fields: fields, index: 3))
}

fn body_pin_index(pins: List<String>) -> Map<String, String> {
  fold(pins |> filter(l => line_is_body_pin(line: l)), init: empty_map(), f: (index, l) => map_insert(m: index, key: body_pin_key(line: l), value: body_pin_value(line: l)))
}

// The declared body changes that excused a row, by row key: the content pair each one bound.
fn excused_body_changes(findings: List<JoinFinding>) -> Map<String, String> {
  fold(findings, init: empty_map(), f: fn(index, f) {
    match f {
      RowBodyChanged { entry: e, function: fn_name, was: w, now: n, declared: declared } =>
        if declared { map_insert(m: index, key: row_key(entry: e, function: fn_name), value: concat(w, "\t", n)) } else { index }
      _ => index
    }
  })
}

fn body_pin_excused(excused: Map<String, String>, line: String) -> Bool {
  match map_lookup(m: excused, key: body_pin_key(line: line)) {
    Present { value: pair } => pair == body_pin_value(line: line)
    Absent => false
  }
}

// A new row against the old observation through the pre-image.
fn new_row_finding(
  preimage: Map<String, String>,
  old_rows: Map<String, String>,
  added_rows: Map<String, Bool>,
  row: ObservedRow
) -> JoinFinding {
  match map_lookup(m: preimage, key: row.entry) {
    Absent => RowIntroduced { entry: row.entry, function: row.function }
    Present { value: was_path } =>
      match map_lookup(m: old_rows, key: row_key(entry: was_path, function: row.function)) {
        Absent => RowGained { entry: row.entry, function: row.function, declared: path_present(index: added_rows, path: row_key(entry: row.entry, function: row.function)) }
        Present { value: _ } => RowPreserved
      }
  }
}

fn old_file_finding(forward: Map<String, String>, new_files: Map<String, Bool>, path: String) -> JoinFinding {
  if path_present(index: new_files, path: carried(forward: forward, path: path)) {
    RowPreserved
  } else {
    FileRemoved { path: path }
  }
}

fn new_file_finding(preimage: Map<String, String>, path: String) -> JoinFinding {
  match map_lookup(m: preimage, key: path) {
    Absent => FileAdded { path: path }
    Present { value: _ } => RowPreserved
  }
}

// The full join. `declared_removals` are old-tree paths the caller names from the independent record of
// the change; `declared_row_removals` are old-side rows (`entry<TAB>function`, the entry the old tree's
// path) the change deletes with the declaration, and `declared_row_additions` are new-side rows the change
// writes (entry the new tree's path). A declaration excuses a row only when the row is actually lost or
// gained, and it is reported beside the row (ROW_LOST_DECLARED, ROW_GAINED_DECLARED), never absorbed; a
// declaration that matches no such row is itself red (DECLARATION_UNUSED), as is one given twice
// (DECLARATION_DUPLICATED), and a function the new file still declares without its marker is a lost marker,
// which the caller does not declare. `declared_unread` are new-tree paths whose channel refusal the caller has found declared
// (a supplied value, so the join judges the shape of the declaration and never reads the live one);
// `plan` is the sweep's own digest of the old tree.
fn witness_set_join(
  old: Observation,
  new: Observation,
  plan: PlanEdges,
  declared_removals: List<String>,
  declared_row_removals: List<String>,
  declared_row_additions: List<String>,
  declared_row_changes: List<String>,
  declared_unread: List<String>
) -> List<JoinFinding> {
  let old_rows = row_index(rows: old.rows)
  let new_rows = row_index(rows: new.rows)
  let new_bodies = body_index(rows: new.rows)
  let changes = body_pin_index(pins: declared_row_changes)
  let old_files = path_index(paths: old.files)
  let new_files = path_index(paths: new.files)
  let declared = path_index(paths: declared_removals)
  let removed_rows = path_index(paths: declared_row_removals)
  let added_rows = path_index(paths: declared_row_additions)
  let covered_unread = path_index(paths: declared_unread)
  let unread = fold(new.unread, init: empty_map(), f: (index, u) => map_insert(m: index, key: u.path, value: path_present(index: covered_unread, path: u.path)))
  let preimages = preimages_of(forward: plan.forward, old_files: old.files)
  let row_findings = concat(
    old.rows |> map(r => old_row_finding(forward: plan.forward, new_files: new_files, new_rows: new_rows, declared: declared, removed_rows: removed_rows, unread: unread, new_bodies: new_bodies, changes: changes, row: r)),
    new.rows |> map(r => new_row_finding(preimage: preimages.index, old_rows: old_rows, added_rows: added_rows, row: r))
  )
  let file_findings = concat(
    old.files |> map(p => old_file_finding(forward: plan.forward, new_files: new_files, path: p)),
    new.files |> map(p => new_file_finding(preimage: preimages.index, path: p))
  )
  let input_findings = concat(
    concat(
      plan.paths |> filter(p => !path_present(index: old_files, path: p)) |> map(p => PlanStale { old_path: p }),
      preimages.collisions |> map(c => PlanCollision { paths: c })
    ),
    concat(
      old.malformed |> map(l => InputMalformed { source: "old", line: l }),
      concat(
        new.malformed |> map(l => InputMalformed { source: "new", line: l }),
        plan.malformed |> map(l => InputMalformed { source: "plan", line: l })
      )
    )
  )
  let excused = excused_body_changes(findings: row_findings)
  let declaration_findings = concat(
    concat(
      declared_row_removals |> filter(l => !line_is_row_key(line: l)) |> map(l => InputMalformed { source: "row_removals", line: l }),
      declared_row_additions |> filter(l => !line_is_row_key(line: l)) |> map(l => InputMalformed { source: "row_additions", line: l })
    ),
    concat(
      declared_row_changes |> filter(l => !line_is_body_pin(line: l)) |> map(l => InputMalformed { source: "row_changes", line: l }),
      declared_row_changes
        |> filter(l => line_is_body_pin(line: l) && !body_pin_excused(excused: excused, line: l))
        |> map(l => RowBodyPinUnused { entry: field_of(fields: split(s: l, delimiter: "\t"), index: 0), function: field_of(fields: split(s: l, delimiter: "\t"), index: 1) })
    )
  )
  concat(concat(row_findings, file_findings), concat(concat(input_findings, declaration_findings), exactness_findings(
    findings: row_findings,
    declared_removals: declared_removals,
    declared_row_removals: declared_row_removals,
    declared_row_additions: declared_row_additions,
    declared_row_changes: declared_row_changes,
    declared_unread: declared_unread,
    unread_paths: new.unread |> map(u => u.path)
  )))
}

// ---- every explanation is exact in both directions ---------------------------------------------------
// A finding is excused only by a declaration that names it exactly (a path, an (entry, function) row key, a
// content pair), and a declaration is accepted only if some finding used it. No explanation is a pattern, a
// directory, a count or a reason: the lists hold keys, so a declaration cannot reach a row it does not name.
// The other direction is here: a declaration that excused nothing (it names a file that was not removed or
// held no enrolled row, a row that was neither lost nor gained, a name given twice) is red, so the lists can
// only shrink and a stale line cannot stand as an explanation for a change that no longer happens.
// An unread declaration is accepted only for a path the new observation itself lists as unread; a roster
// entry whose file the channel reads is therefore red here as well as at the population parse.
fn used_keys(findings: List<JoinFinding>, kind: String) -> Map<String, Bool> {
  fold(findings, init: empty_map(), f: fn(index, f) {
    match f {
      RowInRemovedFile { entry: e, function: _, declared: declared } =>
        if declared && kind == "file_removals" { map_insert(m: index, key: e, value: true) } else { index }
      RowLost { entry: e, function: fn_name, declared: declared } =>
        if declared && kind == "row_removals" { map_insert(m: index, key: row_key(entry: e, function: fn_name), value: true) } else { index }
      RowGained { entry: e, function: fn_name, declared: declared } =>
        if declared && kind == "row_additions" { map_insert(m: index, key: row_key(entry: e, function: fn_name), value: true) } else { index }
      _ => index
    }
  })
}

type DuplicateScan {
  seen: Map<String, Bool>
  reported: Map<String, Bool>
  found: List<String>
}

// The lines a list names more than once, each reported once.
fn duplicated_lines(lines: List<String>) -> List<String> {
  let scanned = fold(lines, init: DuplicateScan { seen: empty_map(), reported: empty_map(), found: [] }, f: fn(acc, l) {
    if path_present(index: acc.seen, path: l) && !path_present(index: acc.reported, path: l) {
      DuplicateScan { seen: acc.seen, reported: map_insert(m: acc.reported, key: l, value: true), found: concat(acc.found, [l]) }
    } else {
      DuplicateScan { seen: map_insert(m: acc.seen, key: l, value: true), reported: acc.reported, found: acc.found }
    }
  })
  scanned.found
}

fn unused_declarations(kind: String, lines: List<String>, used: Map<String, Bool>) -> List<JoinFinding> {
  lines |> filter(l => !path_present(index: used, path: l)) |> map(l => DeclarationUnused { kind: kind, key: l })
}

fn duplicated_declarations(kind: String, lines: List<String>) -> List<JoinFinding> {
  duplicated_lines(lines: lines) |> map(l => DeclarationDuplicated { kind: kind, key: l })
}

fn exactness_findings(
  findings: List<JoinFinding>,
  declared_removals: List<String>,
  declared_row_removals: List<String>,
  declared_row_additions: List<String>,
  declared_row_changes: List<String>,
  declared_unread: List<String>,
  unread_paths: List<String>
) -> List<JoinFinding> {
  let well_formed_removals = declared_row_removals |> filter(l => line_is_row_key(line: l))
  let well_formed_additions = declared_row_additions |> filter(l => line_is_row_key(line: l))
  let well_formed_pins = declared_row_changes |> filter(l => line_is_body_pin(line: l))
  concat(
    concat(
      unused_declarations(kind: "file_removals", lines: declared_removals, used: used_keys(findings: findings, kind: "file_removals")),
      concat(
        unused_declarations(kind: "row_removals", lines: well_formed_removals, used: used_keys(findings: findings, kind: "row_removals")),
        unused_declarations(kind: "unread", lines: declared_unread, used: path_index(paths: unread_paths))
      )
    ),
    concat(
      unused_declarations(kind: "row_additions", lines: well_formed_additions, used: used_keys(findings: findings, kind: "row_additions")),
      concat(
        concat(duplicated_declarations(kind: "file_removals", lines: declared_removals), duplicated_declarations(kind: "row_removals", lines: well_formed_removals)),
        concat(
          concat(duplicated_declarations(kind: "row_additions", lines: well_formed_additions), duplicated_declarations(kind: "unread", lines: declared_unread)),
          duplicated_declarations(kind: "row_changes", lines: well_formed_pins |> map(l => body_pin_key(line: l)))
        )
      )
    )
  )
}

fn reported_findings(findings: List<JoinFinding>) -> List<JoinFinding> {
  findings |> filter(f => match f { RowPreserved => false _ => true })
}

fn red_findings(findings: List<JoinFinding>) -> List<JoinFinding> {
  findings |> filter(f => finding_is_red(finding: f))
}

fn join_summary_lines(old: Observation, new: Observation, findings: List<JoinFinding>) -> List<String> {
  [
    concat("old rows: ", int_to_decimal_string(value: count(old.rows))),
    concat("new rows: ", int_to_decimal_string(value: count(new.rows))),
    concat("unread files: ", int_to_decimal_string(value: count(new.unread))),
    concat("preserved dispositions (old and new side, rows and files): ", int_to_decimal_string(value: count(findings |> filter(f => match f { RowPreserved => true _ => false })))),
    concat("red findings: ", int_to_decimal_string(value: count(red_findings(findings: findings))))
  ]
}

// THE DISPOSITION TABLE, DERIVED. One line per disposition a finding can carry that is not a preservation,
// counted from the findings themselves: the figures a report quotes for what the change deleted, wrote,
// rewrote or could not read are these, never a count typed beside the report. A disposition class with a
// zero count still prints, so a class a reader expects and does not see is a printed zero.
fn disposition_kinds() -> List<String> {
  [
    "ROW_LOST_DECLARED",
    "ROW_GAINED_DECLARED",
    "ROW_IN_REMOVED_FILE_DECLARED",
    "ROW_BODY_CHANGED_DECLARED",
    "ROW_UNREAD_DECLARED",
    "ROW_INTRODUCED",
    "FILE_REMOVED",
    "FILE_ADDED"
  ]
}

fn disposition_table_lines(findings: List<JoinFinding>) -> List<String> {
  disposition_kinds() |> map(k => join(["DISPOSITION", k, int_to_decimal_string(value: count(findings |> filter(f => finding_kind(finding: f) == k)))], "\t"))
}

fn join_result_line(findings: List<JoinFinding>) -> String {
  if count(red_findings(findings: findings)) == 0 { "RESULT\tEQUAL" } else { "RESULT\tNOT_EQUAL" }
}

// ---- effects ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
type TextRead
  = TextReadOk { text: String }
  | TextReadRefused { path: String, cause: String }

fn read_text(path: String) -> TextRead {
  let r = Filesystem.Read(path: path)
  match filesystem_read_outcome(content: r.content, success: r.success, error: r.error) {
    FilesystemReadSucceeded { content: text } => TextReadOk { text: text }
    FilesystemReadRefused { error: cause } => TextReadRefused { path: path, cause: cause }
  }
}

fn write_text(path: String, content: String) -> ProcessExit {
  let w = Filesystem.Write(path: path, content: content)
  if w.success { ExitSuccess }
  else { exit_failure(reason: concat("layout witness join: write failed for ", path, ": ", w.error)) }
}

// THE GOVERNED `.dag` PATHS OF A TRACKED FILE LISTING: under a witness layer root and not excluded by the
// floor's own path policy. These are the files the producer will walk, so each owes it a marker fact.
fn governed_dag_paths(listing: String) -> List<String> {
  split(s: listing, delimiter: "\n")
    |> filter(p => p != "" && ends_with(s: p, suffix: ".dag"))
    |> filter(p => any(xs: witness_layer_roots, predicate: root => starts_with(s: p, prefix: concat(root, "/"))))
    |> filter(p => !floor_discovery_path_excluded(path: p, exclude_substrings: witness_exclusion_substrings()))
}

fn observed_bindings() -> List<SourceRootBinding> {
  [
    SourceRootBinding { tree: V2Tree, host_directory: repository_tree_directory(tree: V2Tree) },
    SourceRootBinding { tree: DagTree, host_directory: repository_tree_directory(tree: DagTree) }
  ]
}

// A governed path as the module file it is: the tree whose directory it sits under, and the path
// beneath that directory.
fn observed_file_ref(path: String) -> Optional<ModuleFileRef> {
  match list_find_first(xs: observed_bindings(), predicate: fn(binding) { starts_with(s: path, prefix: concat(binding.host_directory, "/")) }) {
    Absent => optional_absent()
    Present { value: binding } =>
      optional_present(value: ModuleFileRef {
        tree: binding.tree,
        relative_path: substring(s: path, start: string_length(s: binding.host_directory) + 1, end: string_length(s: path))
      })
  }
}

// A governed file the marker channel cannot read is a located observation (MarkedNamesUnread), not an
// abort: the channel's refusal is a fact about the file, and the join reads it as one. A governed path
// under no bound tree is a fault of the run itself (MarkedNamesUnbound) and stops it.
type MarkedNames
  = MarkedNamesRead { declarations: List<AcquisitionMarkedDeclaration> }
  | MarkedNamesUnread { cause: String }
  | MarkedNamesUnbound { cause: String }

fn marked_names_of(env: AcquisitionEnv, path: String, content: String) -> MarkedNames {
  match observed_file_ref(path: path) {
    Absent => MarkedNamesUnbound { cause: concat(path, ": under no bound tree") }
    Present { value: file } =>
      match acquisition_test_markers(env: env, file: file, content: content) {
        AcquisitionMarkersRead { declarations: declarations } => MarkedNamesRead { declarations: declarations }
        AcquisitionMarkersRefused { cause: cause } => MarkedNamesUnread { cause: cause }
      }
  }
}

type MarkedContent {
  path: String
  name: String
  content: String
}

type MarkedSources
  = MarkedSourcesRead { sources: List<FloorMarkedSource>, contents: List<MarkedContent>, unread: List<UnreadFile> }
  | MarkedSourcesRefused { cause: String }

// One governed file at a time: read it, take the marked declarations its own parse tree carries, keep the
// facts (each declaration's name and content digest) and drop the text, so the memory is the facts and not
// the population.
fn marked_sources_go(
  env: AcquisitionEnv,
  pending: List<String>,
  acc: List<FloorMarkedSource>,
  contents: List<MarkedContent>,
  unread: List<UnreadFile>
) -> MarkedSources {
  match list_head(xs: pending) {
    Absent => MarkedSourcesRead { sources: acc, contents: contents, unread: unread }
    Present { value: path } =>
      match read_text(path: path) {
        TextReadRefused { path: p, cause: c } => MarkedSourcesRefused { cause: concat(p, ": ", c) }
        TextReadOk { text: content } =>
          match marked_names_of(env: env, path: path, content: content) {
            MarkedNamesUnbound { cause: cause } => MarkedSourcesRefused { cause: cause }
            MarkedNamesUnread { cause: cause } =>
              marked_sources_go(
                env: env,
                pending: skip(xs: pending, n: 1),
                acc: acc,
                contents: contents,
                unread: Cons { head: UnreadFile { path: path, cause: cause }, tail: unread }
              )
            MarkedNamesRead { declarations: declarations } =>
              marked_sources_go(
                env: env,
                pending: skip(xs: pending, n: 1),
                acc: Cons { head: FloorMarkedSource { repo_path: path, marked: declarations |> map(d => d.name) }, tail: acc },
                contents: concat(declarations |> map(d => MarkedContent { path: path, name: d.name, content: d.content }), contents),
                unread: unread
              )
          }
      }
  }
}

fn content_index(contents: List<MarkedContent>) -> Map<String, String> {
  fold(contents, init: empty_map(), f: (index, c) => map_insert(m: index, key: row_key(entry: c.path, function: c.name), value: c.content))
}

fn observed_report(listing: String, rows: List<FloorDiscoveryRow>, bodies: Map<String, String>, unread: List<UnreadFile>) -> String {
  join(
    concat(
      concat(
        split(s: listing, delimiter: "\n") |> filter(p => p != "" && ends_with(s: p, suffix: ".dag")) |> map(p => observed_file_line(path: p)),
        unread |> map(u => observed_unread_line(unread: u))
      ),
      rows |> map(r => observed_row_line(row: r, body: body_of(index: bodies, key: row_key(entry: r.entry, function: r.function))))
    ),
    "\n"
  )
}

// The producer refuses a walked file it holds no marker fact for, so a file the channel could not read is
// withheld from the walk by its own full path (a whole-file path policy, as the floor's exclusions are)
// and reported as UNREAD: the producer is never handed an empty list for a file nobody read.
fn observed_rows_of(sources: List<FloorMarkedSource>, contents: List<MarkedContent>, unread: List<UnreadFile>, listing: String, report: String) -> ProcessExit {
  match discover_floor_corpus_rows_from_host_facts(
    source_roots: witness_layer_roots,
    exclude_substrings: concat(witness_exclusion_substrings(), unread |> map(u => u.path)),
    owned_data_records: [],
    marked_sources: sources
  ) {
    FloorDiscoveryRefused { reason: reason } => exit_failure(reason: concat("layout witness join: discovery refused: ", reason))
    FloorDiscoveryAccepted { rows: rows } => observed_rows_written(rows: rows, bodies: content_index(contents: contents), unread: unread, listing: listing, report: report)
  }
}

// Every enrolled row owes the observation the content of the declaration it enrols: a row the producer
// enrols that the channel handed no content for would pair on nothing, so it stops the run rather than
// reading as an empty body.
fn observed_rows_written(rows: List<FloorDiscoveryRow>, bodies: Map<String, String>, unread: List<UnreadFile>, listing: String, report: String) -> ProcessExit {
  let bodiless = rows |> filter(r => !body_present(index: bodies, key: row_key(entry: r.entry, function: r.function)))
  match list_head(xs: bodiless) {
    Present { value: row } => exit_failure(reason: concat("layout witness join: an enrolled row has no declaration content: ", row.entry, " ", row.function))
    Absent => write_text(path: report, content: observed_report(listing: listing, rows: rows, bodies: bodies, unread: unread))
  }
}

fn observed_marked(env: AcquisitionEnv, listing: String, report: String) -> ProcessExit {
  match marked_sources_go(env: env, pending: governed_dag_paths(listing: listing), acc: [], contents: [], unread: []) {
    MarkedSourcesRefused { cause: cause } => exit_failure(reason: concat("layout witness join: cannot read the markers: ", cause))
    MarkedSourcesRead { sources: sources, contents: contents, unread: unread } => observed_rows_of(sources: sources, contents: contents, unread: unread, listing: listing, report: report)
  }
}

// OBSERVE THE TREE THE RUN STANDS IN. `files` is the tree's tracked file list (`git ls-files`), the
// population the file-grain check reads; only its `.dag` paths are carried. Run from the tree's root so
// the floor's own roots resolve there. The rows are the real producer's, enrolled from the markers the
// channel captured and from nothing else.
fn layout_witness_observe(files: String, report: String) -> ProcessExit {
  match read_text(path: files) {
    TextReadRefused { path: p, cause: c } => exit_failure(reason: concat("layout witness join: cannot read ", p, ": ", c))
    TextReadOk { text: listing } =>
      match acquisition_env(layout: repository_storage_layout(), bindings: observed_bindings()) {
        AcquisitionEnvUnprepared { diagnostics: _ } => exit_failure(reason: "layout witness join: the dag grammar did not prepare")
        AcquisitionEnvReady { env: env } => observed_marked(env: env, listing: listing, report: report)
      }
  }
}

// JOIN TWO OBSERVATIONS THROUGH THE SWEEP'S PLAN. Exits success only when no finding is red.
fn layout_witness_join(
  old: String,
  new: String,
  plan: String,
  removals: String,
  row_removals: String,
  row_additions: String,
  row_changes: String,
  report: String
) -> ProcessExit {
  match read_join_inputs(paths: [old, new, plan, removals, row_removals, row_additions, row_changes]) {
    JoinInputsRefused { cause: cause } => exit_failure(reason: concat("layout witness join: cannot read ", cause))
    JoinInputsRead { texts: texts } => joined_report(
      old: observation_of(text: field_of(fields: texts, index: 0)),
      new: observation_of(text: field_of(fields: texts, index: 1)),
      plan: plan_edges_of(text: field_of(fields: texts, index: 2)),
      declarations: Declarations {
        files: lines_of(text: field_of(fields: texts, index: 3)),
        row_removals: lines_of(text: field_of(fields: texts, index: 4)),
        row_additions: lines_of(text: field_of(fields: texts, index: 5)),
        row_changes: lines_of(text: field_of(fields: texts, index: 6))
      },
      report: report
    )
  }
}

fn lines_of(text: String) -> List<String> {
  split(s: text, delimiter: "\n") |> filter(l => l != "")
}

type JoinInputs
  = JoinInputsRead { texts: List<String> }
  | JoinInputsRefused { cause: String }

// Every input file, in the order named; the first one that cannot be read refuses the run with its path.
fn read_join_inputs(paths: List<String>) -> JoinInputs {
  let none_read: List<String> = []
  fold(paths, init: JoinInputsRead { texts: none_read }, f: fn(acc, path) {
    match acc {
      JoinInputsRefused { cause: _ } => acc
      JoinInputsRead { texts: texts } =>
        match read_text(path: path) {
          TextReadRefused { path: p, cause: c } => JoinInputsRefused { cause: concat(p, ": ", c) }
          TextReadOk { text: text } => JoinInputsRead { texts: concat(texts, [text]) }
        }
    }
  })
}

// A channel refusal is declared when gunbc.parse_population_refusals names that file under that exact
// cause (the population parse's own judgment, v2.cli.population_verbs roster_declares), so one
// declaration answers both for the parse and for the markers.
fn unread_is_declared(roster: DeclaredRoster, unread: UnreadFile) -> Bool {
  match observed_file_ref(path: unread.path) {
    Absent => false
    Present { value: file } => roster_declares(roster: roster, key: module_file_key(file: file), cause: unread.cause)
  }
}

// The declaration is read once into its roster. A declaration that names a module twice has no single
// answer for it, so it declares nothing: every unread file then stays a red finding.
fn declared_unread_paths(classes: List<RefusalClass>, unread: List<UnreadFile>) -> List<String> {
  match population_parse_begin(classes: classes, compiler: none, reuse: parse_verdict_reuse_off()) {
    PopulationDeclarationDuplicated { keys: _ } => []
    PopulationBegun { tally: tally } =>
      unread |> filter(u => unread_is_declared(roster: tally.roster, unread: u)) |> map(u => u.path)
  }
}

type Declarations {
  files: List<String>
  row_removals: List<String>
  row_additions: List<String>
  row_changes: List<String>
}

fn joined_report(old: Observation, new: Observation, plan: PlanEdges, declarations: Declarations, report: String) -> ProcessExit {
  let findings = witness_set_join(
    old: old,
    new: new,
    plan: plan,
    declared_removals: declarations.files,
    declared_row_removals: declarations.row_removals,
    declared_row_additions: declarations.row_additions,
    declared_row_changes: declarations.row_changes,
    declared_unread: declared_unread_paths(classes: parse_population_declared_refusal_classes(), unread: new.unread)
  )
  let written = write_text(
    path: report,
    content: join(
      concat(
        concat(join_summary_lines(old: old, new: new, findings: findings), disposition_table_lines(findings: findings)),
        concat([join_result_line(findings: findings)], reported_findings(findings: findings) |> map(f => finding_line(finding: f)))
      ),
      "\n"
    )
  )
  if count(red_findings(findings: findings)) == 0 { written }
  else { exit_failure(reason: concat("layout witness join: ", int_to_decimal_string(value: count(red_findings(findings: findings))), " red findings; see ", report)) }
}

data non_fold_residue_frontier: List<FrontierRow> = [
  FrontierRow { subject: PathSubject { path: "finding_line" }, reason: nfr_reason_one_variant_projection, dissolution: nfr_dissolve_derived_variant_projection },
]
